MainPage.xaml
In the MainPage.xaml file you define the UI for your app. You can add elements directly using XAML markup, or you can use the design tools provided by Visual Studio. The Basic Page template creates a new class called MainPage
(or whatever name you enter) that inherits from Page. It also includes some simple content, like a back button and page title, and provides methods for navigation and state management.
<Page
x:Name="pageRoot"
x:Class="HelloWorld.MainPage"
DataContext="{Binding DefaultViewModel, RelativeSource={RelativeSource Self}}"
xmlns="https://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
xmlns:x="https://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
xmlns:local="using:HelloWorld"
xmlns:common="using:HelloWorld.Common"
xmlns:d="https://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
xmlns:mc="https://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
mc:Ignorable="d">
